ngtcp2-crypto-rustls (1.16.0-1~smallgearlab2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * New function ngtcp2_crypto_rustls_session_peer_certificate: the DER of the
    certificates that the server sent, for curl's pinned public key over
    HTTP/3. It needs librustls-quic 0.15.7+quic2, and the packages that use
    this library depend on this version or a later one (dh_makeshlibs -V).

 -- small-gear-lab <289302950+marie-222@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:10:00 +0900

ngtcp2-crypto-rustls (1.16.0-1~smallgearlab1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging of the ngtcp2 crypto helper for Rustls, which lets
    ngtcp2 (and curl's HTTP/3) use Rustls through rustls-ffi-quic.
  * Built from Ubuntu's ngtcp2 1.16.0 source (crypto/shared.c is the part
    that every ngtcp2 crypto helper shares) and crypto/rustls/, which is
    derived from the quictls helper: its packet protection uses OpenSSL's
    libcrypto, its TLS part calls librustls_quic.

 -- small-gear-lab <289302950+marie-222@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0900
